   "html_text": "In 1810, Bolzano published a booklet entitled Contributions to a better founded presentation of mathematics (Bolzano 1810; Bolzano 2004b) in which he developed his views about the unsatisfactory state of the mathematics of his time and the need for its reform. He proposed a new definition of mathematics as “the science which deals with the general laws (forms) to which things must conform in their existence” (Bolzano 1810, I, §8; Bolzano 2004b: 94), a new division of mathematics into universal m",
   "md_text": "In 1810, Bolzano published a booklet entitled Contributions to a better founded presentation of mathematics (Bolzano 1810; Bolzano 2004b) in which he developed his views about the unsatisfactory state of the mathematics of his time and the need for its reform. He proposed a new definition of mathematics as “the science which deals with the general laws (forms) to which things must conform in their existence” (Bolzano 1810, I, §8; Bolzano 2004b: 94), a new division of mathematics into universal m"
